{
  "id": "Compound::DB00625 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Efavirenz is linked to Cyp2c9 through a series of molecular interactions that involve non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors (NNRTIs). The evidence suggests that Efavirenz, as a member of this class, binds to Cyp2c9 via a shared mechanism with Delavirdine, which itself interacts with Cyp2c9. This binding is supported by the lowest common ancestor (LCA) relationship between Efavirenz and Delavirdine, both classified under the broader category of Organic Heterobicyclic Compounds and Non-Nucleoside Reverse Transcriptase Inhibitors. The presence of a direct interaction between Efavirenz and Cyp2c9, as indicated by the LCA of Efavirenz and Delavirdine, implies a potential regulatory role of Efavirenz in Cyp2c9 activity. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Efavirenz influences Cyp2c9, likely through its interaction with the enzyme's active site or by modulating its expression or activity.",
